# Test: Built-in numeric functions with wrong types (arithmetic family)
# Expected: Error: Function 'add' requires both arguments to be numbers
#
# Note:
# - Integration fail tests stop at the first runtime error, so only the first
#   call executes in the CLI fail suite.
# - The remaining cases provide end-to-end LSP diagnostic coverage for the same
#   built-in type-checking path across all arithmetic built-ins.

call add with "hello", "world"         # both wrong
call add with 1, "world"               # number + string
call add with "hello", 2               # string + number
call subtract with "hello", 1          # wrong first arg
call multiply with true, 2             # wrong first arg (bool)
call divide with 8, "two"              # wrong second arg
call power with null, 3                # wrong first arg (null)
